Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:06:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(tts/pocket): cut oversized sentences at more kinds
 of punctuation and balance word splits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- splitAtClauseBoundaries: dashes, ellipses and the edges of a bracketed aside are clause boundaries alongside , ; : — hyphenated words, numeric ranges and punctuation trailing a closing bracket stay whole
- splitAtWordBoundaries: text needing n parts aims each at a 1/n share of its tokens instead of filling to the limit, so no short tail is stranded ("…the first drops hit" + "the pavement.")
- splitSentences: a run of sentence punctuation ("...", "?!") ends one sentence once, so the text reaches the model as written
- normalizeText: a trailing dash is stripped from a sentence-start chunk as trailing , ; : already are
